Revision 1 — 2026-05-14
=========================================================

Summary
---------------------------------------------------------
Fixed 5 bugs: ANSI escape typo, two cursor bounds overruns,
missing key handlers (ENTER/BACKSPACE/DEL/TAB), and a
symbol-name mismatch between syntax.h and syntax.c.

Detail
---------------------------------------------------------

[1] render.c — Wrong ANSI escape code
    Before : "\x1b[k"  (lowercase k)
    After  : "\x1b[K"  (uppercase K)
    Why    : CSI K (Erase in Line) is the standard ANSI
             sequence to clear from cursor to end of line.
             Lowercase k is non-standard and silently ignored
             by Windows Terminal, causing line-clearing to
             silently fail and old characters to remain on
             screen.

[2] input.c — Cursor-down out-of-bounds crash
    Before : cursor_y < screen_rows - 1
    After  : cursor_y < num_rows - 1
    Why    : The old check limited cursor movement by screen
             height, not file content height. Pressing down
             past the last file row then typing would access
             row[cursor_y] when cursor_y >= num_rows →
             out-of-bounds read → crash.

[3] input.c — Cursor-right wrong boundary
    Before : cursor_x < screen_cols - 1
    After  : cursor_x < row->size  (guarded by cursor_y < num_rows)
    Why    : Cursor should stop at the end of the current
             line's content, not the screen edge. The old
             check let the cursor float past line content,
             causing visual desync and confusing insertion
             positions.

[4] ENTER / BACKSPACE / DELETE / TAB keys unhandled
    Files : input.c + editor.c + editor.h
    What  :
      - Added editor_delChar()              — backspace
      - Added editor_deleteCharAtCursor()   — delete key
      - Added editor_insert_newline()       — enter
      - Added editor_insert_tab()           — tab
      - Bound all four to g_key_bindings[]
    Why    : These keys were defined in the EditorKeys enum
             but had no action functions or binding entries,
             making them silent no-ops at runtime.

[5] syntax.c — Symbol-name mismatch with syntax.h
    Before : g_highlight_data_base[], g_highlight_db_entries
    After  : g_high_light_data_base[], g_high_light_data_base_entries
    Why    : syntax.h declared extern names with "high_light"
             and "data_base_entries", but syntax.c defined
             them as "highlight" and "db_entries". Linker
             would fail with "unresolved external symbol".

Affected Files
---------------------------------------------------------
  src/render.c      —  1 line changed
  src/input.c       — 12 lines changed
  src/editor.c      — 110 lines added
  src/editor.h      —  1 line added
  src/syntax.c      —  2 lines changed

