Revision 4 — 2026-05-15 (Post-review bugfix)
=========================================================

Summary
---------------------------------------------------------
Fixed editor_insert_newline cursor position bug: pressing Enter
at the start of a line (cursor_x == 0) caused cursor_y to
advance twice, skipping the new empty line.
---------------------------------------------------------
Detail
---------------------------------------------------------

[1] src/editor.c — editor_insert_newline cursor skip on cursor_x==0
    Before :
      if (cursor_x == 0) { insert_raw(ec, cursor_y, "", 0); }
      cursor_y++;  // always runs — wrong for cursor_x==0
    After  :
      if (cursor_x == 0) { insert_raw(ec, cursor_y, "", 0); }
      else { /* split row ... */ cursor_y++; }
      cursor_x = 0;
    Why    : When cursor_x==0, insert_raw inserts an empty row
             AT cursor_y, pushing the current content row down.
             The cursor should stay on the empty line. Running
             cursor_y++ unconditionally skipped past it to the
             content row below, causing an off-by-one: the line
             the user was on appeared visually empty, the next
             line showed the typing destination, and the first
             line scrolled off the terminal.

Affected Files
---------------------------------------------------------
  src/editor.c            —  5 lines changed

